            }
          },
          "required": [
            "kind",
            "target_id",
            "reachable"
          ],
          "type": "object"
        },
        {
          "description": "A payload kind this build does not know.\n\nSerde's untagged-fallback position: it must be **last**, and it captures\nthe tag so a client can log what it skipped. Without it, a Phase 1 UI\nwould hard-fail on the first Phase 5 event."
        }
      ],
      "description": "The event payloads.\n\nInternally tagged on `kind`, so an unknown payload is distinguishable from a\nmalformed one and a client can log \"kind=x, ignored\" instead of failing.\nAdding a variant is a minor bump; a client built earlier must tolerate one it\ndoes not know, which is why [`EventPayload::Unknown`] exists."
    },
    "EventStream": {
      "description": "The named event streams.\n\nA closed enum on purpose: a client subscribes by name, and an unknown stream\nname should be a clear error at subscribe time rather than a silent\nnever-delivers. Adding a stream is a minor bump.",
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "const": "job",
          "description": "Job queue transitions (§6 Phase 1's queue core).",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "scan",
          "description": "Scan and walk progress.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "index",
          "description": "Index build progress.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "tier",
          "description": "Tiering, verification and restore progress.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "power",
          "description": "Power and network state changes (Phase 4 populates it; the stream is\ndeclared now so the Dashboard's contract does not change then).",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "target",
          "description": "Target reachability and scrub results.",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ]
    },
    "Seq": {
      "description": "A monotonic per-daemon-run event sequence number.\n\nNumbering is **global across streams**, not per stream. One counter means a\nclient holds one cursor no matter how many streams it subscribes to, and the\nrelative order of a `ScanProgress` and the `JobTransition` it caused is\npreserved. The cost is that a client subscribed to one stream sees gaps in\nthe numbers it receives; that is expected and is why the contract is \"no\ngaps in what the daemon *emitted*\", not \"no gaps in what you received\".\n\nSequence numbers restart at 1 on daemon restart. A resume cursor is\ntherefore only meaningful within one run, which is why\n[`SubscribeResult::epoch`] exists.",
      "format": "uint64",
      "minimum": 0,
      "type": "integer"
    }
  },
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "description": "One event, as delivered.\n\nSent as a JSON-RPC notification (`method: \"event\"`, no `id`), which is what\nlets events share the connection with request/response traffic.",
